WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.570
A knock at the door.

2
00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.670
Your friend is hiding upstairs.

3
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.970
The man outside wants to kill her.

4
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.070
He asks you where she is.

5
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:13.190
In 1797, Kant answered a critic
who had raised this very case.

6
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.680
Kant built his ethics on duty.

7
00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.500
Can it cope with hard cases like this?

8
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.280
In this mission, you'll
build an argument map:

9
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:25.090
the strongest points for Kant,
and the hardest points against.

10
00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.730
Then you'll weigh the critics against
the replies his defenders give,

11
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.170
and try a hard case of your own.

12
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:35.790
Your mission: weigh up whether Kant's
ethics can cope with cases like this.
